;; The shipped ROLE MAP: which file serves each role a project's workflow has.
;;
;; A project's first run copies this to .samizdat/userspace.edn, with every file
;; it names, and from then on the PROJECT's copy is the map: src/ asks for a
;; role — :loop, :policy-tool, :gates — and the map says which file answers.
;; Nothing in src/ lists what a project has. The agent may point a role at a
;; different file, add roles of its own, or drop ones it no longer uses; a
;; role src/ asks for that the map does not have is refused, and the agent is
;; told which role and where to add it.
;;
;; Paths are relative to .samizdat/ (and, here, to resources/). Cells are a
;; LIST, loaded in this order, because a later cell registering an id wins.

{:manifests
  {:loop "manifests/loop.edn"
   :beam "manifests/beam.edn"
   :critic "manifests/critic.edn"
